+- [Should-fix] §3 Downgrade ("At `Stop`, if `terminationReason`/`error` shows an injection error"); §3 Version handling ("the Stop-hook downgrade covers breaking releases"); §3 Doctor list — The Stop-hook downgrade detects only abort-style injection errors. A future agy that silently ignores the undocumented `systemMessage` step (as it already does for unknown keys) produces no Stop error, so delivery stops silently: no downgrade, no doctor signal, and pull seats get no digest fallback. The Version handling claim overstates the mechanism's coverage.
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: Root Background line 60: "A well-formed unsupported step aborts the turn. Malformed output is silently ignored together with any valid sibling steps." Downgrade trigger (line 223) fires only on a Stop injection error. Doctor list (lines 247-252) has no "offered N times, never confirmed" item. Line 176: the check-in omits digest "always for pull", so a HookPull seat has no in-context fallback. Line 254: "the Stop-hook downgrade covers breaking releases." Delivery-policy design lines 57 and 252-254 park an item after 3 unconfirmed offers and name "an injection agy silently dropped" as a case that waits for `inbox`. Scouts cite probe 09-unknownkey: `{"injectSteps":[{"bogusKey":1}]}` returned SUCCESS with an empty Stop error.
