+decision: patch
+summary: Round 1, no recurrence yet. The 24 findings are mostly independent local defects. A few share a cause and can be fixed by rule: the agy hook's client-local state-file handling, ledger state loss, the attention block, fail-open hooks that drop their diagnostics, and docs that describe the state before this branch. None of these comes from a design decision that would justify a redesign. The parked and untested Must-fix items need the human or a test run, not a design change.
+pattern: Nothing recurs, since this is the first round. The confirmed findings group around five spots. (1) The agy hook's per-conversation and downgrade state files, `src/harness/agy/delivery.rs`, use a lock-free, always-fsync read-modify-write: r1 [Nit] src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:873; src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:880, r1 [Nit] src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:647; src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:644, r1 [Nit] src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:830. (2) The process-local offer ledger drops state: r1 [Nit] src/delivery/ledger.rs:137, r1 [Nit] src/delivery/ledger.rs:96. (3) Fail-open hook paths discard every error signal: r1 [Nit] src/cli/hook.rs:2878, r1 [Nit] src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:325. (4) The DeliveryPull attention block: r1 [Should-fix] src/service/delivery_pull.rs:294, r1 [FYI] src/service/delivery_pull.rs:297. (5) Docs and comments still describe the pre-branch state. These are separate local rules, not one weak decision showing up in several places. The client-local hint-file design is sanctioned by TRUST-POLICY A2 and by design §Pull step 2. Moving that state into the daemon would cost more than the three Nits it removes. The highest-severity finding, r1 [Should-fix] src/store/lazy_delivery.rs:249 (the wake frontier is keyed on staging order rather than publication order), stands alone and has a local fix.
+clusters:
+- agy-state-files: r1 [Nit] src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:873; src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:880, r1 [Nit] src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:647; src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:644, r1 [Nit] src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:830 | rule: send every agy adapter-state file write (conversation state and downgrade.json) through one helper. That helper reuses `harness::manifest::write_private` with a parent-create option instead of the duplicate. It holds an advisory flock around load-mutate-save, skips the write when the serialized bytes are unchanged, does not fsync these A2 hint files, and has a prune pass that rotates its scan start and also removes `.tmp*` leftovers. Every caller in delivery.rs moves onto it: confirm/remove_downgrade, pre_invocation probation, stop, and prune_if_new. If a lock is not wanted, the race goes into the design's accepted limits instead.
+- ledger-monotonic: r1 [Nit] src/delivery/ledger.rs:137, r1 [Nit] src/delivery/ledger.rs:96 | rule: no ledger mutation may lose offer accounting. A write from an older generation is ignored and never wipes a newer entry. An id that has reached MAX_OFFERS_PER_GENERATION is kept as a parked marker instead of being evicted. Apply this in `seat_mut` and `SeatOffers::record`, and check that every other ledger write site follows the same rule.
+- hook-silent-failures: r1 [Nit] src/cli/hook.rs:2878, r1 [Nit] src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:325 | rule: fail-open means empty stdout, not lost signal. `HookStep::run` returns an optional diagnostic that is threaded into `HookOutcome.diagnostic`. Every swallowed error in the agy step reports through that channel or through a last-failure record the doctor reads: no daemon, no claim, refused pull, failed confirm, and state or downgrade write failures.
+- attention-block: r1 [Should-fix] src/service/delivery_pull.rs:294, r1 [FYI] src/service/delivery_pull.rs:297 | rule: build the attention block's command from `marker_prefix`, in both the pull path and the watch path (cli/watch.rs). Pin it with service tests for three cases: block present, block absent when `seen_current`, and an attention-only page that answers Page.
+- stale-docs: r1 [Nit] src/protocol/delivery.rs:1; src/protocol/delivery.rs:3, r1 [Nit] TRUST-POLICY.md:211, r1 [FYI] src/harness/agy/setup.rs:379, r1 [Nit] src/service/delivery_pull.rs:384, r1 [Nit] src/harness/agy/plugin.rs:60, r1 [Must-fix] docs: agent-usage.md handoff kinds, TRANSCRIPT_WINDOW doc comment, claude/permissions.rs:37 doc comment, sweep DP10 'unchanged' claim | rule: make one pass over every doc and comment the branch touched, plus any that name a harness list or a capability state, and make each describe shipped behaviour. That covers advertised capabilities, `ANTIGRAVITY_AGENT` in the marker lists (also docs/agent-usage.md:5/:79, docs/operations.md:221, and the ~/.gemini entry in AGENTS.md:10), the not-atomic-CAS wording, confirm replay answering not_offered, the agy downgrade note in install.md and the agy README, and the misplaced or garbled doc comments.
