@@ -0,0 +1,213 @@
+super-roast verdict: Should-fix (24 confirmed)
+mode: pr        iteration: 1 of 3
+profile (assumed): Open-source developer tooling (herdr-threads, a Rust CLI/daemon, v0.6.0 public) used locally by a single user to coordinate coding agents in Herdr panes. The trust model is same-user and cooperative (TRUST-POLICY). Correctness of seat continuity, receipts, delivery settlement and user-config ownership matters; writes to user config must be owned and reversible. No network-exposed surface, no multi-tenant data, easy local rollback.
+inputs: super-auto/agy-harness-adapter@539f0637 vs main@f3431b31
+coverage: scouts 12/12 (correctness, security, premortem, simplicity-design, hot-path-perf, concurrency-async, data-migrations, deploy-safety, api-contract, observability, testing, hygiene-docs) · raw 94 → deduped 85 → panel 46 · spot 38 · promoted 1 · judge completion 100% · remainder-capped: 0
+independence: same-family (Claude) — seat-differentiated panel · rung: Workflow
+seat-agreement: panels 47 · rr 0.74 · rg 0.81 · fg 0.77 · unanimous 0.66 · ground-loo 0.89 (n=35) · reproduce 23/24/0 · refute 17/30/0 · ground 28/19/0
+lane-yield (found/confirmed/unique/refuted): correctness 7/3/1/4 · security 8/1/1/7 · premortem 7/3/2/4 · simplicity-design 12/0/0/5 · hot-path-perf 7/2/2/5 · concurrency-async 6/3/2/3 · data-migrations 2/2/1/0 · deploy-safety 7/3/1/4 · api-contract 11/4/3/7 · observability 6/3/3/3 · testing 10/3/3/3 · hygiene-docs 11/1/1/5
+
+## Confirmed findings
+- [Should-fix] src/store/lazy_delivery.rs:249 — The persisted lazy wake frontier `wake_work.last_lazy_ordinal` stores a staging-order AUTOINCREMENT ordinal, but rows become visible at publication. A lazy send staged earlier and published later gets an ordinal at or below an already-stored frontier, so a `wake_on: all` seat is never woken for it until a higher ordinal arrives. [lanes: data-migrations]
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: migrations/0026:20 `ordinal INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT`, assigned by `stage_recipient` (src/store/lazy_delivery.rs:290) during the audience walk, before any manifest exists. `walk_audience` (src/store/messages.rs:481) stages in bounded multi-transaction quanta, so two preparations interleave. `wake_frontier`/`pending_summary` (lazy_delivery.rs:231-251) return `max(ordinal)` over published rows only; `reserve` (src/store/wake.rs:522) and `complete_with_pokes` (wake.rs:694-702) persist it; `has_unreserved_lazy` (src/ports.rs:2351) is `pending_lazy() > last_reserved_frontier.lazy`. `note_published` (lazy_delivery.rs:281) bumps reason_bits only and never moves the frontier. Trace: A stages ordinal 5, B stages 6 and publishes, seat woken, frontier=6, A publishes, Some(5) > Some(6) is false, no wake. All three seats found no compensating mechanism; TRUST-POLICY A8 (lines 444-456) does not accept missed wakes. Column is new in this branch (schema.rs:606, migration 0029).
+  fix-shape hint: key the frontier on publication order (e.g. decision_seq or the published row's sequence) instead of staging ordinal, or have `note_published` lower/reset the stored frontier when the newly published row's ordinal is at or below it.
+
+- [Should-fix] src/service/delivery_pull.rs:294 — The attention block DeliveryPull adds when `other_pending > 0` and the version moved (DP5 step 5) is never asserted by any service, hook or integration test. [lanes: testing]
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: src/service/delivery_pull.rs:294-297 `with_attention = !seen_current && view.fingerprint.other_pending > 0` pushes a FrameItem of kind "attention". Design DP5 step 5 (delivery-policy-design.md:242) requires it. Greps across tests/service, tests/scheduler, tests/cli, tests/harness, tests/hook_entrypoint found no pull-page assertion on an attention block; `other_pending` appears in tests/service/delivery_pull.rs only at line 697 inside the fingerprint-hash test. The `kind == "attention"` assertions in tests/integration/mod_delivery.rs (1129, 1882, 2605) exercise the watch/push channel, a different code path. Untested: block present with pending invitation/warning, block absent when `seen_current`, attention-only page answers Page not Unchanged (depends on `blocks.is_empty()` ordering).
+  fix-shape hint: add service tests that seed a pending invitation or waking warning for a hook-pull seat and assert the three cases (present, absent on `seen_current`, attention-only page is `Page`).
+
+- [Nit] src/delivery/ledger.rs:137 — A DeliveryPull or DeliveryConfirm that read the binding before a generation rotation can write the ledger after a newer-generation request created its entry; `seat_mut` deletes on any generation mismatch, wiping the current generation's offered set. [lanes: concurrency-async]
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute REJECT (outvoted) / ground ✓)
+  evidence: ledger.rs ~137 `if entry.generation != generation { self.seats.remove(seat) }` with no older/newer check. delivery_pull.rs:211 reads `binding` via `hook_pull_view`, drops the lock for `drain_pages`, re-locks at :304 with the stale binding; delivery_confirm does the same at :362/:387/:432. Consequence: a later gen2 confirm finds no offers, answers `NotOffered` (:454), ids are re-offered as new. Refute seat rejected citing delivery-policy-design.md:55/249 (at-least-once, rotation discards the ledger by design); the majority already weighs that: no message lost, a duplicate offer and a missed settle only. Default stands.
+  fix-shape hint: make `seat_mut` ignore or refuse a write whose generation is below the stored one (monotonic guard).
+
+- [Nit] src/delivery/ledger.rs:96 — With more than 256 pending items whose confirmations do not settle, the per-seat offer cap evicts unconfirmed offers; evicted ids come back as brand-new offers with count 1, so the 3-offer cap and 60 s spacing are bypassed and every PreInvocation injects a fresh page. [lanes: premortem]
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: `SeatOffers::record` (ledger.rs:96-107) evicts oldest by `first_at` past MAX_OFFERS_PER_SEAT=256, dropping count/last_at. delivery_pull.rs:262 skips only `known.get(id).is_some_and(|o| !o.is_due(now))`, so an evicted id is shown again. `more_pending` disables the Unchanged shortcut (:313); `next_pull` returns `Delivers` at `offers.len() >= 256` (ledger.rs:64, comment "An evicted pending id would be shown again"). Delivery-policy design line 57 states re-offers are bounded and DP5 rejects unbounded re-injection. Trigger needs >~288 pending plus persistently failing confirms.
+  severity note: reproduce seat rated Should-fix, refute and ground rated Nit. Kept at Nit: profile states a single-user local tool; the impact is repeated context injection (cost), not data loss, and it needs a double fault.
+  fix-shape hint: never evict ids whose count has reached MAX_OFFERS_PER_GENERATION (keep a parked set or high-water marker), or stop pulling when the ledger is at cap.
+
+- [Nit] src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:873; src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:880 — The shared downgrade.json (and per-conversation state) is read-modify-written by concurrent agy hook processes with no lock or compare-and-swap, so misses, downgrades, probation and removals can be lost or resurrected. [lanes: correctness, concurrency-async]
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: `stop()` (~861-890) loads via `self.downgrade()`, mutates, `save_downgrade` → `write_private` (231-257), a `tmp<pid>` temp file plus rename. `pre_invocation` sets probation and saves (~848); `confirm` calls `remove_downgrade` (734). No flock/CAS in src/harness/agy/. Interleavings: two Stops each append a miss, later rename wins; a Stop saves a stale probation record after another conversation's confirm removed the file. docs/superpowers/runs/.../code-final-review-6.md:84 already lists this under "Deferred OK". Self-heals via 24 h probation or `setup agy`.
+  fix-shape hint: take an advisory flock on downgrade.json around the load-mutate-save, or document the accepted race in the design's accepted limits.
+
+- [Nit] src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:647; src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:644 — The conversation-state prune examines only the first 256 readdir entries with no cursor, so past 256 files stale entries behind fresh ones are not pruned, and `.tmp<pid>` leftovers are never pruned. [lanes: correctness, premortem]
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute REJECT (outvoted) / ground ✓)
+  evidence: delivery.rs:647 `read_dir(...).flatten().take(PRUNE_SCAN_LIMIT)` with PRUNE_SCAN_LIMIT=256 (line 50), no cursor; called only from prune_if_new (773). Extension check at 649 skips non-`.json`. Module doc (lines 10-12) promises "a file untouched for 30 days is deleted when another conversation's file is created". Refute seat rejected as "delayed, not forever"; the majority concedes pruning is delayed rather than unbounded but the doc promise and the .tmp gap remain. Each file is at most 4 KiB.
+  fix-shape hint: rotate the scan start (random or persisted cursor) and include `.tmp*` leftovers; or state the 256-entry bound in the module doc.
+
+- [Nit] src/harness/agy/delivery.rs:830 — Every agy top-level PreInvocation rewrites the conversation state file through `write_private`, which calls `File::sync_all` before rename, even on the `Unchanged` reply where the bytes did not change. On macOS `sync_all` is F_FULLFSYNC. [lanes: hot-path-perf]
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: `pre_invocation` Unchanged arm (~830) calls `state.save` unconditionally; `save` (323) → `write_private` (231) does write_all, `sync_all` (248), rename; no changed-bytes check. `turn` only increments at invocation 0, so later steps rewrite identical bytes. External fact grounded by two seats from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/library/std/src/sys/fs/unix.rs: `#[cfg(target_vendor = "apple")] unsafe fn os_fsync(fd) { libc::fcntl(fd, libc::F_FULLFSYNC) }`. src/cli/journal.rs:1935 records the repo already treating F_FULLFSYNC cost as a problem. File is a client-local hint (A2).
+  fix-shape hint: skip the save when the serialized bytes equal what was loaded, and drop `sync_all` for this hint file.
+
+- [Nit] src/cli/hook.rs:2960 — On every agy top-level PreInvocation the hook scans the pane's context-journal directory twice (pane_session closure in decode_refined, then pane_context_snapshot in run_hook_step), each opening and parsing up to 256 journals. Before this diff the scan ran only on rare DeclaredReset events. [lanes: hot-path-perf]
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: decode_refined (hook.rs:2777) builds a `pane_session` closure calling `pane_context_snapshot`; agy `witness::local_evidence` (src/harness/agy/witness.rs:111-146) invokes it whenever the presence marker is Present. run_hook_step (hook.rs:2845) calls `pane_context_snapshot` again in the same process. Both go through `pane_context_journal` (hook.rs:2962). On main neither helper exists; the only scan was in `record_observer_reset`. Bounded by the deadline and a 50 ms per-journal cap.
+  fix-shape hint: pass the snapshot computed in decode_refined through to run_hook_step instead of recomputing it.
+
+- [Nit] scripts/agy-sandbox/fetch-agy:124 — `fetch-agy` uses the manifest's `version` string unvalidated as a path component, so a version containing `../` writes the extracted executable and manifest.json outside `--dest`. [lanes: security]
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute REJECT (outvoted) / ground ✓)
+  evidence: parse_manifest (lines 59-66) checks only non-empty str; install() (119-127) does `Path(dest) / version; mkdir(parents=True); write_bytes; chmod 0o755`. `--version` only has to equal the manifest's own value. Script is manual-only, refuses CI, writes only files named `agy` and `manifest.json`, and whoever controls the manifest already controls the binary the user runs. No privilege-escalation floor applies: same user, no new reach.
+  fix-shape hint: reject a version containing a path separator or `..`, e.g. require `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` and not `.`/`..`.
+
